  "diagnosis_text": "**Diagnosis:** the inter-switch link **s3 port 1 \u2194 s4 port 2** is down.\n\n**Evidence**\n- `h1 \u2192 h5` ICMP fails completely: **5/5 packets lost**.\n- ONOS topology reports only 4 of the 5 configured ring links; the missing link is **s3\u2013s4**.\n- Port state confirms both ends are disabled:\n  - `s3-eth1` (peer `s4:2`): **enabled=false**\n  - `s4-eth2` (peer `s3:1`): **enabled=false**\n- The direct physical `s1:2 \u2194 s5:1` link and their host-facing ports are enabled, so this is not a local h1/s1 or h5/s5 attachment failure.\n\n**Why this breaks h1\u2013h5:** the installed baseline forwarding rules send traffic for h5 from s1 out **port 1 toward s2**, and return traffic for h1 from s5 out **port 2 toward s4**. Those paths require the s3\u2013s4 segment, which is down. The available direct s1\u2013s5 link is not selected by these installed flows.\n\n**Localisation / next step:** investigate and restore the **s3-eth1 / s4-eth2** link (or correct/recompute the forwarding policy to use `s1\u2013s5` as the alternate path). I cannot make that repair from here.",
